  {
    "n": 28,
    "tag": "h1",
    "text": "Unicode",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 29,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Support UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32 encodings, including little endian and big endian.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 30,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "These encodings are used in input/output streams and in-memory representation.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 31,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Support automatic detection of encodings in input stream.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 32,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Support transcoding between encodings internally.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 33,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "For example, you can read a UTF-8 file and let RapidJSON transcode the JSON strings into UTF-16 in the DOM.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 34,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Support encoding validation internally.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 35,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "For example, you can read a UTF-8 file, and let RapidJSON check whether all JSON strings are valid UTF-8 byte sequence.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 36,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "Support custom character types.",
    "tokens": []
  },
  {
    "n": 37,
    "tag": "li",
    "text": "By default the character types are {1} for UTF8, {2} for UTF16, {3} for UTF32.",
